WEBVTT

00:02.600 --> 00:06.900
So I've been working on this application called GBook.

00:07.300 --> 00:09.400
I've been using Claude to make it.

00:10.200 --> 00:13.600
And so if you go to my GitHub page and open the releases,

00:13.800 --> 00:16.300
you can see some release details over there.

00:16.600 --> 00:21.100
I have it available for Linux, Windows, as well as for Android.

00:21.300 --> 00:23.600
You can download the APK here,

00:24.000 --> 00:28.800
and you can join the test list for the Play Store.

00:28.900 --> 00:31.900
It's not public yet. You can only join in as a tester.

00:32.200 --> 00:35.000
And you can send me your email if you want to check it out.

00:35.400 --> 00:38.000
So basically, this is how the application looks like.

00:38.300 --> 00:40.200
The reason why I made this application is

00:40.300 --> 00:45.400
because I've been struggling to find a good ebook reader.

00:46.000 --> 00:49.000
And one of my biggest challenges and problems

00:49.000 --> 00:53.000
has been around how applications have been parsing PDFs.

00:53.800 --> 00:57.700
So for instance, in most applications, if you open a PDF,

00:57.900 --> 01:00.900
for instance, this book over here, The Bitcoin Standard.

01:01.200 --> 01:06.100
If I open it as a PDF, this is how it looks like on most books.

01:06.300 --> 01:08.800
Now, this is hard to read and even to keep track,

01:08.900 --> 01:13.300
even trying to highlight stuff or trying to zoom into the text.

01:13.500 --> 01:17.900
And so with this application, you can just press here, Reflow.

01:18.900 --> 01:23.900
And there it comes, just like how ebooks are being parsed.

01:24.400 --> 01:28.700
You can even highlight easily, select the text that you want to highlight.

01:31.100 --> 01:39.000
And so, apart from this, one of the other reasons why

01:43.300 --> 01:48.600
I like this new application that I'm using right now to read the books that I'm reading

01:49.100 --> 01:51.900
is this reading tracker.

01:52.100 --> 01:55.300
So for instance, whenever I'm reading, sometimes you get lost

01:55.300 --> 01:58.000
and forget maybe where you were reading,

01:58.000 --> 02:00.800
or struggle to focus on the specific line that you're reading.

02:01.100 --> 02:03.700
So this reading tracker over here, you can enable it over here,

02:03.700 --> 02:05.800
and you can set it to be at the middle or at the bottom.

02:06.000 --> 02:09.900
The reason for having it at the bottom is, for instance, if you have a very large screen,

02:10.100 --> 02:12.700
even if you prefer, it depends on where your thumb is,

02:12.800 --> 02:15.500
where you prefer to have your thumb when you're using your phone.

02:15.700 --> 02:18.400
So for instance, it can become very, very easy

02:18.600 --> 02:22.700
to just read through and track where you're reading.

02:22.900 --> 02:25.900
So you just scroll like that, from the top to the bottom,

02:26.200 --> 02:29.400
and keep on moving this highlighter.

02:29.600 --> 02:30.900
And you can even change this as well.

02:31.200 --> 02:34.700
So for instance, if I just come over here and use, like, green,

02:34.900 --> 02:39.300
if I come back over here, now we're using green to highlight what I'm reading.

02:39.500 --> 02:43.500
So yeah, this is one of the features I like about it.

02:43.600 --> 02:46.000
And also, you can even track goals.

02:46.100 --> 02:50.800
So for instance, let's say I'm reading this book over here,

02:51.100 --> 02:54.500
A Culture of Growth, here.

02:58.500 --> 03:01.300
So for instance, over here I can see,

03:01.500 --> 03:04.900
I personally use a 30-minute-a-day reading goal.

03:05.200 --> 03:08.600
So I can even see how many minutes are left to complete that goal.

03:08.800 --> 03:10.300
And if I'm done, I'm done.

03:10.500 --> 03:12.200
And here I can just see all my reading activities

03:12.400 --> 03:15.600
of the books that I've been reading, for 30 days, for seven days.

03:16.000 --> 03:17.700
I can even create a plan for reading a book.

03:17.800 --> 03:24.400
Let's say I want to read this book maybe for...

03:25.000 --> 03:27.900
I can put, like, 30 minutes.

03:28.100 --> 03:31.200
I can even add here a reminder of what time I want to be reading.

03:31.600 --> 03:35.000
I can even set, for instance, a goal for...

03:35.300 --> 03:43.200
I can set a goal for how long I want to read that book for.

03:43.800 --> 03:46.300
So for instance, I can open it over here

03:46.500 --> 03:48.300
and I can say, add a reading plan.

03:49.000 --> 03:53.600
And I can say that I want to read this book maybe within three months, or within a year.

03:54.200 --> 03:56.800
So for instance, this book is very, very long.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.600
So it would take a very long time to complete.

03:58.800 --> 04:00.200
It has almost a thousand pages.

04:00.800 --> 04:04.900
So I can just pick how long I want to read this book for.

04:05.100 --> 04:07.200
And then I can just keep track of it.

04:07.500 --> 04:10.900
And even the app will be reminding you that you have to keep on reading this book.

04:11.000 --> 04:16.000
And so you can even import your books just from Google Drive easily.

04:16.500 --> 04:20.000
And we're also still working on having this Google Drive backup,

04:20.400 --> 04:24.900
so you can be able to read between your desktop application

04:25.400 --> 04:27.300
at the same time, like, reading on your phone.

04:27.300 --> 04:29.200
You just proceed from where you left off.

04:29.400 --> 04:30.900
So we're still working on that.

04:31.100 --> 04:33.900
And another feature that I like about this application is the feed section.

04:34.300 --> 04:36.700
So for instance, the highlights that I make for my book,

04:36.800 --> 04:39.100
or even just posting directly what I've highlighted,

04:39.400 --> 04:44.400
I can make these cool posters that I can just be reading through.

04:44.500 --> 04:47.000
Let's say, for instance, that you're in the class

04:47.200 --> 04:50.200
and you don't want to read the whole book,

04:50.200 --> 04:52.700
but you just want to do a recap to see what you've been reading about the book,

04:52.800 --> 04:57.400
and try to pull out the core concepts that you would like to remember about the book.

04:57.600 --> 05:01.400
So I can just open this feed section and read through it.

05:01.900 --> 05:07.900
Yeah, so you can check me if you want to get access to the application,

05:08.300 --> 05:11.000
or if you think there's some changes that you can make

05:11.100 --> 05:16.600
to make it even better than what it looks like right now,

05:16.800 --> 05:17.700
you can just tell me.

05:17.800 --> 05:19.100
And it's even open source.

05:19.200 --> 05:24.000
You can even clone it and do whatever you want to do with the application.

05:36.500 --> 05:41.300
Made with ❤️ · props to Ame
